# cutlass_receipt's kernels, one cutlass_receipt_kernel.cu object each (job.sh's cgemm stage):
# name cfg var rounds p mode [spread [grain [extra [honest [forced [xvar [fvar]]]]]]]   (cfg 0 prefill, 1 decode; var 0 alu, 1 imad; L = 128 p / grain;
# mode 0 plain, 1 receipt, 2 dump, 3 extra only; spread 1 interleaves the receipt over the k-tile's four k-blocks; grain 2
# or 4 receipts every chain after every second or every 32-deep k-block; extra X adds a cheater's X alu phi1 steps a thread
# after every 32-deep k-block, on chains of its own; honest H gives the first H chain words of each receipt point one more
# round; forced F adds F phi1 steps after every 32-deep k-block on receipt chains that read no accumulator; xvar 1 makes
# the cheater's steps imad phi1 (`_xiX` in the name), xvar 2 FFMAs (`_xfX`), xvar 3 an alu phi1 and six FFMAs each
# (`_xmX`); fvar 2 makes the forced steps FFMAs, `_ffF`)
